Grand Junction Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2333 UTC Wednesday, July 30, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 527 PM MDT Wed Jul 30 2025

Scattered showers and a few thunderstorms will continue to

impact areas over the higher terrain through 03z, before

tapering off. Skies will clear overnight as drier air starts to

filter in. Another round of showers and thunderstorms are

expected over the terrain tomorrow afternoon. The main threats

continue to be gusty outflow winds, hail, and lightning, with a

lesser chance of brief heavy rain. Occasional drops to MVFR/IFR

conditions will be possible if any of these showers or storms

move directly over an airport. Westerly winds gusting 20-30

knots are expected at lower elevation terminals tomorrow

afternoon. Smoke from regional wildfires will filter in

overnight, impacting terminals in eastern Utah, and far western

Colorado.





