North Platte Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2333 UTC Wednesday, July 30, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 629 PM CDT Wed Jul 30 2025

VFR conditions last through the evening across western and north 

central Nebraska, however stratus will continue to build in from the 

west throughout the evening and night. As the stratus builds in, 

conditions will worsen from MVFR down to LIFR. Fog is expected to 

develop, particularly across southwest Nebraska into central 

Nebraska in the predawn hours, given the ample moisture and light 

surface winds. As better mixing develops by mid morning, conditions 

should gradually recover to MVFR, becoming VFR by the afternoon. 





