Goodland Aviation Discussion

Issued at 0016 UTC Thursday, July 31, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 611 PM MDT Wed Jul 30 2025

For KGLD & KMCK... VFR conditions are forecast for the beginning

of the period through about 09Z. Around that time, enough

moisture should have moved into the area for ceilings to begin

lowering, though it could take until 12Z before ceilings lower

below 3000ft. If ceilings lower early, they likely would lower

to around 500ft at both site by 12-14Z. Otherwise, they would

likely only lower to 1500ft by 12-14Z. Fog is another potential

concern, though it is forecast to be more spotty in nature due

to the cloud ceilings keeping dewpoint depressions around 3-5

degrees. While the current TAF calls for 4-6SM, be aware that

1/4SM is possible, especially if ceilings lower to a few hundred

feet. By 18Z, ceilings and fog should lift with VFR conditions

through the remainder of the period.



Dodge City Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2235 UTC Wednesday, July 30, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 533 PM CDT Wed Jul 30 2025

A slow moving frontal boundary located in the Oklahoma panhandle

will keep chances of storms mainly around LBL through the

evening and a forecast complex of storms moving southeast out of

Colorado could bring VCTS to LBL through the overnight.

Otherwise post frontal clouds will continue to keep cloud

ceilings hovering around MVFR category through 17-18Z.  





