Amarillo Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2247 UTC Wednesday, July 30, 2025



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 540 PM CDT Wed Jul 30 2025

A weather system is moving across the panhandles that is producing

rain showers and thunderstorms that may impact all terminals. This

afternoon and overnight the storms are more likely to impact KAMA

and KDHT with a lesser chance for KDHT. During the passage of

these storms conditions may drop to IFR due in large to heavy

rainfall dropping visibilities. There is a very low chance that

the storms become strong to severe with large hail and damaging

wind gusts. The storms have a moderate chance of continuing

through the overnight hours before ceasing leaving a quite mid to

late morning Thursday. Further rain showers and thunderstorms are

anticipated to form during Thursday afternoon and evening with

broadly the same impacts.  





