Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 0006 UTC Thursday, July 31, 2025



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 604 PM MDT Wed Jul 30 2025

Storms across southwest and central NM will look to fill into the

lower RGV this evening. Meanwhile, a backdoor front will push

through eastern NM focusing shower and thunderstorm coverage

across the east central and southeast plains and south central

mountains overnight. Low clouds could develop in the wake of this

activity heading towards sunrise Thursday. Another crop of showers

and thunderstorms will develop midday across the Gila Mountains, 

northern mountains and south central mountains. Storms will be 

capable of producing heavy rainfall, gusty and erratic winds and 

small hail resulting in some brief MVFR to IFR conditions across 

central TAF sites. Meanwhile, some gusty and erratic wind gusts 

possible at KGUP from nearby virga showers.



